  "body": "Updated to Vim 9.2.1252\n\n[![MacVim release-184 download](https://img.shields.io/github/downloads/macvim-dev/macvim/release-184/MacVim.dmg?label=macOS%2010.13%2B)](https://github.com/macvim-dev/macvim/releases/download/release-184/MacVim.dmg) [![MacVim release-184 download (10.9-10.12)](https://img.shields.io/github/downloads/macvim-dev/macvim/release-184/MacVim_10.9.dmg?label=macOS%2010.9-10.12)](https://github.com/macvim-dev/macvim/releases/download/release-184/MacVim_10.9.dmg)\n\nThis release mostly brings the Vim version up to date.\n\nAnnouncements\n====================\n\nMoving macOS 10.13 - 11.0 support to legacy release\n--------------------\n\nThe next binary release of MacVim will require macOS 12.0 Monterey or above for the normal version. Users of macOS 10.13 - 11.0 will need to use the legacy version instead. If you are updating MacVim via the builtin updater, this should work automatically. For the most part this should be a transparent change for those users, except for an older updater (Sparkle 1).\n\nNote that the last MacVim release made a similar announcement but we never ended up bumping the min requirement.\n\nGeneral\n====================\n\n- Sparkle (updater for MacVim) is now updated to 2.9.6. #1702\n\nNew Vim Features\n====================\n\n- Modeline now defaults to a limited subset of whitelisted options ([`:h 'modelinestrict'`](https://macvim.org/docs/redirect.html?tag='modelinestrict')). [v9.2.0350](https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/4c287947164fe26a6bd32e1c9362668388ae7457)\n    - Note: This change is slightly backwards incompatible. If you want to open files with modelines using non-whistlisted options, you will need to turn it off by adding `:set nomodelinestrict` to your vimrc.\n- Popup images ([`:h popup-image`](https://macvim.org/docs/redirect.html?tag=popup-image)). This works in terminals that support displaying images. MacVim will support this in a later version. [v9.2.0612](https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/9d9bad24ad3721f55c5369131b68eb6896f17af1)\n- new bundled color scheme:\n    - novum, port of Neovim's dev_theme (vim/vim#20723)\n- Clickable regions in the statusline, tabline and tabpanel with the new %[FuncName] item.\n- Misc tab panel and tab line improvements.\n- Fixes the stray \"pp\" that shows up when opening Vim in terminal. [v9.2.0389](https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/44f707da6a06b8310bfe23f5477c7653215e1230)\n- Misc performance improvements and security fixes.\n- Other platforms (these don't affect MacVim and included for reference only):\n    - Support for GTK 4 on Linux. [v9.2.0501](https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/da5ebe71cbf56a89796000fa1aa92f6a76acf4c7)\n\n\n<details><summary>Compatibility</summary>\n\nCompatibility\n====================\n\nRequires macOS 10.9 or above. (10.9 - 10.12 requires downloading a separate legacy build)\n\nScript interfaces have compatibility with these versions:\n\n- Lua 5.5\n- Perl 5.34\n- Python2 2.7\n- Python3 3.9 or above\n- Ruby 4.0\n\n</details>\n",
